# Git commits — no Cursor co-author

When creating or amending commits for this repository:

- **Never** add `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>` or any other `Co-authored-by` line for Cursor or the agent.
- Commit messages contain only the subject, optional body, and optional `✅ Closes: #<n>` footer per `AGENTS.md` — nothing else in the trailer block.

If a tool or environment tries to append a Cursor co-author trailer, omit it and commit with a clean message only.

The `.husky/commit-msg` hook removes that trailer if it is injected anyway.
